<title>FRANCE: French soldier killed in Yugoslavia road mishap.</title>
<headline>French soldier killed in Yugoslavia road mishap.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A French soldier working on a road construction project in the Gorazde area of eastern Bosnia was killed when the ground caved in under an excavating machine that he was driving, the army said on Friday.</p>
<p>The machine overturned, instantly killing Private First Class Nicolas Paradis, a member of a French field engineers batallion attached to the NATO-led Implementation Force (IFOR), the army said. The mishap occured late on Thursday.</p>
</text>
